# Quectel modems (VID 2c7c): make sure the USB network function comes up as ECM
# (AT+QCFG="usbnet",1) and not RNDIS, which we have no host driver for.
#
# Matched on the parent USB device so it fires once per plug-in instead of once
# per serial interface. The switch itself runs as a systemd oneshot, because the
# modem has to be reset afterwards and udev must not be blocked that long.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="2c7c", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="quectel-ecm.service"

# Once the modem is in ECM mode its network function shows up as a separate net
# device (renamed to wwan0 by 79-quectel-ecm-name.rules). Nothing else in the
# image would configure it, so start the DHCP client from here.
#
# This only has to fire once, when the device first appears: quectel-ecm-up.service
# is BindsTo= the wwan0 device unit with Restart=always, so it survives the modem
# re-enumerating and stops when the modem is really unplugged. It used to be a
# oneshot that this rule had to re-trigger on every re-enumeration, which does not
# work - SYSTEMD_WANTS only creates a job when the device unit *transitions* into
# active, and it does not transition across a modem reset. See the unit for the
# full story.
SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2c7c", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="quectel-ecm-up.service"
